gfx1100/ROCm: offload MoE-router GGML_OP_SUM_ROWS to the CPU backend

The standalone reduce_rows_f32 kernel launch used for the MoE router top-k
weight normalization (the RESHAPE->SUM_ROWS->CLAMP->DIV->RESHAPE path taken
whenever the router is not handled by the fused topk-moe kernel, e.g. with the
production `-ot ffn_gate_inp=CPU`) fails AQL dispatch on gfx1100 (RX 7900 XT)
with hipErrorIllegalState:

    ShaderName : void reduce_rows_f32<false>(float const*, float*, int)
    rocvirtual.cpp:3650: Pcie atomics not enabled, hostcall not supported
    rocvirtual.cpp:3990: AQL dispatch failed!
    hipLaunchKernel: Returned hipErrorIllegalState
    ggml-cuda.cu: ROCm error: the operation cannot be performed in the present state
      in function ggml_cuda_kernel_launch at common.cuh <- ggml_cuda_op_sum_rows

This is NOT a launch-dimension overflow: the failing launch is grid {168,1,1},
block {32,1,1}. The reduce_rows_f32 code object requires hostcall services that
are unavailable because PCIe atomics are not enabled on this root complex, so
the runtime rejects the dispatch. Reporting GGML_OP_SUM_ROWS as unsupported on
the HIP backend makes the ggml scheduler run that one tiny reduction on the CPU
backend while every other op stays on the GPU -- which `-ot` cannot express (it
moves tensors, not ops). See README.md in this directory for full diagnosis.

Diagnosed 2026-06-26 on llama.cpp HEAD 3fc4e105 (sci-misc/llama-cpp-9999, guru
overlay), ROCm 7.2, gfx1100, under dev-debug/gdb[rocm]+AMD_LOG_LEVEL=3. Remove
once fixed upstream or once PCIe atomics / hostcall work on this hardware.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu
@@ -5432,6 +5432,19 @@
             return true;
 #endif
         case GGML_OP_SUM_ROWS:
+#if defined(GGML_USE_HIP)
+            // gfx1100/ROCm workaround: the standalone reduce_rows_f32 launch used for
+            // the MoE router top-k weight normalization fails AQL dispatch with
+            // hipErrorIllegalState ("operation cannot be performed in the present
+            // state"). That kernel's code object requires hostcall services which are
+            // unavailable on this PCIe topology ("Pcie atomics not enabled, hostcall
+            // not supported"), so the dispatch is rejected. Force GGML_OP_SUM_ROWS onto
+            // the CPU backend (the reduction is tiny); everything else stays on GPU.
+            // Local llama-cpp overlay patch -- drop once fixed upstream/by hardware.
+            return false;
+#else
+            return ggml_is_contiguous(op->src[0]);
+#endif
         case GGML_OP_MEAN:
         case GGML_OP_GROUP_NORM:
             return ggml_is_contiguous(op->src[0]);
